      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance? mostly looking for stuff on color contrast ratios and making sure screen readers work right for a new fintech app we're building",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "WCAG 2.1 compliance, a crucial step in ensuring your fintech app is accessible to all users, including those with visual impairments. A good checklist should include:\n\n1. **Color Contrast Ratio**: Ensure that the main content has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 against the background. You can use the WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio checker tool to verify this. For example, if you're using a dark background with white text, the contrast ratio should be at least 4.5:1. A good rule of thumb is to use the 60-70% rule: if 60-70% of the text is on a lighter background, the contrast ratio is sufficient.\n2. **Screen Reader Compatibility**: Test your app with popular screen readers like JAWS, NVDA, and VoiceOver. Ensure that all interactive elements, such as buttons, links, and form fields, are announced correctly by the screen reader. You can also use the WAVE Web Accessibility Evaluation Tool to identify potential issues.\n3. **Keyboard Navigation**: Ensure that all interactive elements can be accessed using a keyboard. This includes buttons, links, and form fields. You can test this by using the keyboard to",
      "source": "target",
